---
layout: base.njk
bare: true
title: "Sign up"
referrer: "origin-when-cross-origin"
description: "Create an Inflowwww agency owner account with a username and a password, nothing else. Each agency on the app sees only its own creators."
---
{#- Follows signup.infloww.com (docs/infloww-landing-snapshot.md §8): dark, form left, pitch right, same field order.
    Email address becomes the app's username. The form signs up on the app itself (auth.njk). No Turnstile: their
    "Let us know you're human" box is a struck-through line. -#}
{%- from "auth.njk" import authForm, usernameField, passwordField, submitButton, handoffNote, logo, badges, notice with context -%}
<div class="min-h-dvh bg-[#121212]">
  <div class="wrap pt-5">{{ logo() }}</div>
  <div class="wrap grid gap-14 pt-10 pb-16 sm:pt-14 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-16 lg:gap-24 lg:pt-20 lg:pb-24">
    <section aria-labelledby="signup-title" class="w-full max-w-lg">
      <h1 id="signup-title" class="text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-[43px]">Sign up</h1>
      {%- call authForm("register") %}
        {{ usernameField("name.agency", true) }}
        {{ passwordField("new-password", "Create a password", "Must be at least 6 characters", true) }}

        <div class="mt-6 flex items-start gap-3">
          {#- No name: the box is checked in the browser and never sent. -#}
          <input id="agree" type="checkbox" required class="auth-check mt-1.5" />
          <label for="agree" class="text-lg text-white/85">
            I agree to the <a class="auth-underline" href="{{ '/legal/privacy/' | url }}">Privacy Policy</a> and
            <a class="auth-underline" href="{{ '/legal/terms/' | url }}">Terms of Service</a>
          </label>
        </div>

        {#- Their Cloudflare Turnstile box. Phones get no tooltip; the screen-reader text says the same. -#}
        <p class="mt-8 text-base text-white/70">
          <span class="line-through" title="No CAPTCHA on this page.">Let us know you're human</span><span class="sr-only"> (No CAPTCHA on this page.)</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">We'll take your word for it.</span>
        </p>

        <div class="mt-6">{{ submitButton("Sign up without email") }}</div>
        {{ handoffNote() }}
      {%- endcall %}
      <p class="mt-8 text-base text-white/85">
        Already have an account? <a class="auth-link" href="{{ '/login/' | url }}">Log in</a>
      </p>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-white/60">Chatters don't sign up here. They join through an invite link from their agency's owner.</p>
    </section>

    {#- Facts: docs/routes.md "Sign-in (app)", agencies and their creators. -#}
    <section aria-labelledby="signup-pitch" class="md:pt-6">
      <h2 id="signup-pitch" class="text-[clamp(2.25rem,4vw,3.75rem)] leading-[1.08] font-semibold tracking-tight text-balance">
        Accelerate your agency's success. Not ours.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-xl text-pretty text-white/90">
        Sign up and access every built feature for 7 days, then the 7 after that, and so on—no credit card needed,
        because there is no card form. Get started in just two fields.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-xl text-base text-pretty text-white/60">
        One Inflowwww app serves many agencies. Each owner signs up with their own username, chatters get their own
        logins through their owner's invite, and each agency account sees only its own creators and their chats (the
        one exception is in the <a class="auth-underline" href="{{ '/legal/privacy/' | url }}">Privacy Policy</a>).
      </p>
      {{ badges() }}
    </section>
  </div>
  {{ notice() }}
</div>
